tus":"candidate"},{"name":"Laura Pelant","party":null,"status":"candidate"}],"scope":"school","level":"School","area":"Monticello","schoolNum":"0882"},{"id":"mn-wright-sd0883-school-board-member-isd-883-elect-3","office":"School Board Member (ISD #883) (Elect 3)","category":"School Board Member (ISD #883) (Elect 3)","seats":3,"type":"nonpartisan","description":"","ballotOrder":5000,"candidates":[{"name":"Jamie Hillstrom","party":null,"status":"candidate"},{"name":"Eric Gordee","party":null,"status":"candidate"},{"name":"Amy Smith","party":null,"status":"candidate"},{"name":"Beth Praska","party":null,"status":"candidate"}],"scope":"school","level":"School","area":"Rockford","schoolNum":"0883"},{"id":"mn-wright-sd0885-school-board-member-isd-885-elect-3","office":"School Board Member (ISD #885) (Elect 3)","category":"School Board Member (ISD #885) (Elect 3)","seats":3,"type":"nonpartisan","description":"","ballotOrder":5000,"candidates":[{"name":"Tyler Hemmesch","party":null,"status":"candidate"},{"name":"Tim Lewis","party":null,"status":"candidate"},{"name":"Brent Harapat","party":null,"status":"candidate"}],"scope":"school","level":"School","area":"St Michael-Albertville","schoolNum":"0885"},{"id":"mn-wright-sd2687-school-board-member-isd-2687-elect-3","office":"School Board Member (ISD #2687) (Elect 3)","category":"School Board Member (ISD #2687) (Elect 3)","seats":3,"type":"nonpartisan","description":"","ballotOrder":5000,"candidates":[{"name":"Shannah Mulvihill","party":null,"status":"candidate"},{"name":"Katie Anne Koch","party":null,"status":"candidate"},{"name":"Tristin Michael Fliehe","party":null,"status":"candidate"}],"scope":"school","level":"School","area":"Howard Lake-Waverly-Winsted","schoolNum":"2687"},{"id":"mn-wright-sd2859-school-board-member-isd-2859-elect-3","office":"School Board Member (ISD #2859) (Elect 3)","category":"School Board Member (ISD #2859) (Elect 3)","seats":3,"type":"nonpartisan","description":"","ballotOrder":5000,"candidates":[{"name":"Elizabeth Griebel","party":null,"status":"candidate"},{"name":"Anthony Paggen","party":null,"status":"candidate"},{"name":"Chad Moser","party":null,"status":"candidate"},{"name":"Sarah Hueser","party":null,"status":"candidate"},{"name":"Joyce Peterson","party":null,"status":"candidate"},{"name":"Donna VonBerge","party":null,"status":"candidate"},{"name":"Kevin Kuester","party":null,"status":"candidate"},{"name":"Timothy Dilworth","party":null,"status":"candidate"}],"scope":"school","level":"School","area":"Glencoe-Silver Lake","schoolNum":"2859"}],"referendums":[{"id":"mn-amendment-1","name":"CONSTITUTIONAL AMENDMENT 1: Increasing funding to school districts","type":"Ratification Of State Constitutional Amendment","statewide":true,"ballotLanguage":"Shall the Minnesota Constitution be amended to increase the funding going to all school districts from the permanent school fund, which is a fund that supports school districts without raising individual income or property taxes, effective July 1, 2027?"},{"id":"mn-wright-11818-township-question-1-clearwater-twp","name":"TOWNSHIP QUESTION 1 (Clearwater Twp): Approval of Option B","type":"Local Public Question","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"Shall Option B, providing for the appointment of the clerk by the town board, be adopted for the government of the town?\n\nMinnesota Statutes, sections 367.30 and 367.31 provide for optional forms of town government and one of the options (Option B) allows the Town to seek the transition of treasurer position from an elected office to an appointed office","mcds":["11818"]},{"id":"mn-wright-sd0728-school-district-question-1-isd-728","name":"SCHOOL DISTRICT QUESTION 1 (ISD #728): School District Question 1  Approval of Bond Issue and Capital Project Levy Authorization","type":"Local Public Question","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"The school board of Independent School District No. 728 (Elk River Area Schools) has proposed a project for the acquisition and betterment of school sites and facilities, including the construction and equipping of a new high school and early childhood through middle school building in Otsego, Minnesota^ the construction and equipping of an education center to serve alternative high school learners and children with disabilities^ the construction of safety improvements and secure entrances at school sites and facilities, including at the Zimmerman Middle/High School and Rogers Middle School^ the construction and equipping of a classroom addition at the Hassan Elementary School^ remodeling and updates to the career and technical education (CTE) spaces in Zimmerman, Elk River and Rogers^ repair and renovation projects at school sites and facilities^ the acquisition, installation, replacement, support and maintenance of software, educational software, software licenses, computers, improved technology equipment, networks, infrastructure, the costs of technology related personnel and training^ the acquisition of curriculum, textbooks and materials^ utility services costs and other capital revenue purposes. To provide funds for a portion of the project costs, the school board has proposed to issue general obligation school building bonds in an amount not to exceed $350,000,000. To provide funds for the remaining portion of the project costs, the school board has proposed a capital project levy authorization in the amount of 5.579% times the net tax capacity of the school district. The proposed capital project levy will raise approximately $9,000,000 for taxes payable in 2027, the first year it is to be levied, and would be authorized for ten (10) years. The estimated total cost of the projects to be funded by the capital project levy authorization is approximately $90,000,000. The projects to be funded have received a positive review and comment from the Commissioner of Education.\n\nShall the issuance of the general obligation school building bonds and the capital project levy authorization proposed by the school board of Independent School District No. 728 be approved?\n\nBY VOTING \"YES\" ON THIS BALLOT QUESTION, YOU ARE VOTING FOR A PROPERTY TAX INCREASE.","schoolNum":"0728","area":"Elk River Area"},{"id":"mn-wright-sd0881-school-district-question-1-isd-881","name":"SCHOOL DISTRICT QUESTION 1 (ISD #881): Approval of Capital Project Levy Authorization","type":"Local Public Question","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"The school board of Independent School District No. 881 (Maple Lake Public Schools) has proposed a capital project levy authorization of 1.5841% times the net tax capacity of the school district. The additional revenue from the proposed authorization will be used to provide funds for the acquisition and betterment of school sites and facilities^ deferred maintenance^ the acquisition and maintenance of software, technology, and technology systems, and to pay the costs of technology-related personnel and training^ the acquisition of curriculum, textbooks, and materials^ and other operating capital revenue purposes. The proposed capital project levy authorization will raise approximately $195,000 for taxes payable in 2028, the first year it is to be levied, and would be authorized for ten years. The estimated total cost of the projects to be funded over that time period is approximately $1,950,000.\n\nShall the capital project levy authorization proposed by the school board by Independent School District No. 881 be approved?\n\nBY VOTING ''YES\" ON THIS BALLOT QUESTION, YOU ARE VOTING FOR A PROPERTY TAX INCREASE.","schoolNum":"0881","area":"Maple Lake"},{"id":"mn-wright-sd2859-school-district-question-1-isd-2859","name":"SCHOOL DISTRICT QUESTION 1 (ISD #2859): Revoking Existing Referendum Revenue Authorization^  Approving New Authorization","type":"Local Public Question","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"The school board of Independent School District No. 2859 (Glencoe-Silver Lake Public Schools) has proposed to revoke the school districts existing referendum revenue authorization of $601.98 per pupil and to replace that authorization with a new authorization of $1,445 per pupil. The proposed referendum revenue authorization would be applicable for ten years commencing with taxes payable in 2027, and increase each year by the rate of inflation beginning with taxes payable in 2028, unless otherwise revoked or reduced as provided by law.\n\nShall the school districts existing referendum revenue authorization be revoked, and the increase in the revenue proposed by the school board of Independent School District No. 2859 be approved?","schoolNum":"2859","area":"Glencoe-Silver Lake"}]}